 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS A.\nO sweet old Tower of Judah! O,\nA tomb that bared the pillars away,\nAnd, bearing all thy dead in thy shadow,\nThou girt thou art to love and sorrow!\nNo wretched remains to thy unsorrowed walls,\nOr scattered ashes on thy lone plateau;\nNot even a remnant of former,\nWhere thy strong citadel shook before;\nBut was not cast aside for ever,\nSince the footsteps fell upon the altar?\nTo-day is thy very fate disgraced: never",
